{"name":"Fabric of Space","hex":"#341758","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fabric","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edifice or building.","The act of constructing, construction, fabrication."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with fabric."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fabric"},{"term":"space","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Unlimited or generalized extent, physical or otherwise.\nThe distance between objects. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The distance between objects. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To roam, walk, wander.","To set some distance apart."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/space"}],"entries":[{"title":"Textile","blocks":[{"text":"A textile is any of various fibre-based materials, including fibres, yarns, filaments, threads, and different types of fabric. Originally, textiles were woven; however, weaving is not the only manufacturing method, and many other methods were later developed to form textile structures based on their intended use. Knitting and non-woven are other popular types of fabric manufacturing. In the contemporary world, textiles satisfy the material needs for versatile applications, from simple daily clothing to bulletproof jackets, spacesuits, doctor's gowns and technical applications like geotextiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Warp_in_Progress.jpg/330px-Warp_in_Progress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Textile"},{"title":"Space","blocks":[{"text":"Space is a three-dimensional continuum containing positions and directions. In classical physics, physical space is often conceived in three linear dimensions. Modern physicists usually consider it, with time, to be part of a boundless four-dimensional continuum known as spacetime. The concept of space is considered to be of fundamental importance to an understanding of the physical universe. However, disagreement continues between philosophers over whether it is itself an entity, a relationship between entities, or part of a conceptual framework."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/3D_coordinate_system.svg/330px-3D_coordinate_system.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg/500px-Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg/1280px-Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg/500px-Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Handmade floral patterns on textiles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg/1280px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut